# Line-ending normalization. This repo is developed on Windows but builds/runs on Linux
# (CI runners, Docker images). Without this, a CRLF<->LF flip silently changes a file's bytes.
#
# For Flyway migrations this is not cosmetic: Flyway records a CHECKSUM per applied migration and
# fails the app at boot if a previously-applied file's checksum changes. A line-ending normalization
# of an already-shipped *.sql migration would therefore break startup on staging/prod while every
# fresh dev/CI database stays green. Pin migrations (and all SQL) to LF so the checksum is stable
# regardless of the author's OS or git autocrlf setting.

# Let git decide for unmarked files (normalizes to LF in the repo, checks out native on Windows).
* text=auto

# Force LF in the working tree too for these — never CRLF, on any platform.
*.sql   text eol=lf
*.sh    text eol=lf
*.yml   text eol=lf
*.yaml  text eol=lf

# Binary assets — never normalize.
*.png   binary
*.jpg   binary
*.jpeg  binary
*.gif   binary
*.ico   binary
*.pdf   binary
*.jar   binary
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
